# vscode → harrix-notes-explorer commit

When any changes are made under `vscode/` in this repo (`harrix-swiss-knife`):

1. Commit locally in `harrix-swiss-knife` as usual per `# Git style` (agent-touched files only; never push).
2. At the end of the response, explicitly remind that a matching commit is also needed in `D:\GitHub\harrix-notes-explorer`.
3. Suggest a commit message for **that** repo using the same commit-prefix style as usual.
4. Do not run git commands in `harrix-notes-explorer` unless the user explicitly asks.

## Reminder format

End with the local commit result for this repo, then the reminder and suggested title for the other repo. Labels as plain text above; **only the commit message** in inline backticks. Example:

Commit (harrix-swiss-knife):

`a1b2c3d 🔧 Modify preview-copy styles in vscode extension`

Also commit in D:\GitHub\harrix-notes-explorer:

Commit (harrix-notes-explorer):

`🔧 Modify preview-copy styles`

If the change only lives under `vscode/` and mirrors into the public extension, still always print the `harrix-notes-explorer` commit line so it is not forgotten.
